WEBVTT

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:10.808
Cold, patronizing, arrogant...

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:11.970
I know she can be difficult.

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.570
"Difficult"?
She's impossible.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.308
I'm getting tired
of playing referee

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:17.213
every time you two
have a disagreement.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.343
If you have a problem,
talk to her yourself.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.217
Does the word "irrelevant"
mean anything to you?

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.516
She won't listen.

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:24.318
She may look human,
she may sound human,

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.619
but she's all Borg.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.489
Part of the problem
is your attitude.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.551
You've never tried

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.495
to accept Seven
as part of the crew.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.554
And with good reason.

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:32.826
Guess what she did this morning.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:33.992
She took an isolinear processor

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.465
out of Engineering
without asking,

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:37.561
and when I went to Astrometrics
to get it back,

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.765
she had locked the door...
like that lab

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.330
is her own private domain.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.534
What do you want me to do?

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.907
Throw her in the brig
for the rest of the trip home?

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.673
I've heard worse ideas.

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.908
Seven of Nine to Chakotay.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:49.937
Chakotay here.

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:52.247
Report to the Astrometrics Lab
at once.

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:53.752
On my way.

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:54.754
Did you hear that?

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:55.914
She's giving orders now.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:59.186
I'm telling you, Chakotay,
if she gets in my way again,

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.250
I am not responsible
for what happens.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.560
You're a senior officer
on this ship.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:05.723
Act like one.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.323
Find a way to deal with her.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.705
Astrometrics?

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:16.709
I've been summoned.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.142
Any guesses what this is about?

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:19.509
None.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.646
Your call sounded urgent.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:25.912
It was.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.476
I've been working
to increase the range

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.987
of the astrometric sensors

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:29.987
and I've detected something

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.648
that you should find
of particular interest.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.124
A ship.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.490
What's special about it?

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:37.394
I've analyzed
the warp signature.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.557
It's a Starfleet vessel.

00:03:39.217 --> 00:03:41.117
The ship we're seeing is
in the Alpha Quadrant.

00:03:41.152 --> 00:03:42.278
You couldn't have extended

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.844
the astrometric sensors
that far.

00:03:43.888 --> 00:03:45.617
No, but I increased
the range far enough

00:03:45.657 --> 00:03:47.955
to detect a large network
of relay stations.

00:03:47.992 --> 00:03:49.357
They are alien in origin,

00:03:49.394 --> 00:03:50.986
abandoned,
but still functioning.

00:03:51.029 --> 00:03:52.894
By establishing a sensor link
with the nearest station,

00:03:52.931 --> 00:03:54.865
I'm getting readings
from the entire network.

00:03:54.899 --> 00:03:56.594
The Starfleet ship
is within range

00:03:56.634 --> 00:03:57.828
of one of the farthest sensors

00:03:57.869 --> 00:03:59.894
near the outer edges
of the Alpha Quadrant.

00:04:01.906 --> 00:04:04.500
It must be
on a deep-space mission.

00:04:04.542 --> 00:04:06.601
I've extrapolated its course.

00:04:06.644 --> 00:04:07.941
It doesn't look
like we'll be able

00:04:07.979 --> 00:04:09.503
to keep track of it very long.

00:04:09.547 --> 00:04:11.947
The ship should move
out of range in 41 minutes.

00:04:11.983 --> 00:04:14.178
Can we use the network
to transmit a message?

00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:16.687
Yes, but we'll have
to remodulate our signal

00:04:16.721 --> 00:04:18.188
to match the network's
interlink frequency.

00:04:18.223 --> 00:04:19.622
We don't have much time.

00:04:19.657 --> 00:04:21.352
Get it done, Chakotay.

00:04:33.171 --> 00:04:34.798
Seven of Nine to Ensign Kim.

00:04:34.839 --> 00:04:36.238
Kim here.

00:04:36.274 --> 00:04:39.835
I'm sending you
the interlink frequencies.

00:04:40.845 --> 00:04:41.812
Got it.

00:04:41.846 --> 00:04:43.711
Seven, how much longer
do we have?

00:04:43.748 --> 00:04:44.976
16 minutes.

00:04:45.016 --> 00:04:45.983
That should do it.

00:04:46.017 --> 00:04:47.279
The sub-space

00:04:47.318 --> 00:04:50.310
transceiver is at 200 percent
output and on line.

00:04:50.355 --> 00:04:51.322
We're ready.

00:04:51.356 --> 00:04:52.721
Open a channel.

00:04:52.757 --> 00:04:54.190
Open.

00:04:54.225 --> 00:04:56.193
Starfleet vessel...

00:04:56.227 --> 00:05:00.527
this is Captain Kathryn Janeway
of the Starship Voyager.

00:05:00.565 --> 00:05:02.499
We are in the Delta Quadrant

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:09.531
at coordinates
18 mark 205 mark 47.

00:05:09.574 --> 00:05:13.032
Remodulate your signal to match
our interlink frequency.

00:05:18.816 --> 00:05:21.284
We're receiving a transmission.

00:05:21.318 --> 00:05:22.649
Let's hear it.

00:05:23.688 --> 00:05:26.851
...Starship Voyager.

00:05:26.891 --> 00:05:28.358
We are in the...

00:05:28.392 --> 00:05:31.953
...at coordinates 18...

00:05:32.063 --> 00:05:33.360
Bridge to Seven.
What went wrong?

00:05:34.498 --> 00:05:36.363
I don't understand.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.664
My readings show that the
station picked up our message

00:05:38.703 --> 00:05:40.694
and relayed it
across the entire network.

00:05:40.738 --> 00:05:42.296
We should try widening
the subspace bandwidth

00:05:42.339 --> 00:05:43.670
and sending the message again.

00:05:43.708 --> 00:05:44.697
Do it.

00:05:44.742 --> 00:05:46.141
Transmitting.

00:05:46.177 --> 00:05:48.145
The signal is being relayed.

00:05:48.179 --> 00:05:50.977
No sign of interference.

00:05:52.283 --> 00:05:53.978
Wait. It's being deflected
back again.

00:05:54.018 --> 00:05:57.784
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway
of the Starship Voyager.

00:05:57.822 --> 00:06:01.485
...the Delta Quadrant
at coord...

00:06:01.525 --> 00:06:03.550
I have a possible
explanation, Captain.

00:06:03.594 --> 00:06:05.391
As our carrier wave moves
along the network,

00:06:05.429 --> 00:06:07.056
it may be degrading.

00:06:07.098 --> 00:06:09.293
Can we try
a different kind of signal?

00:06:09.333 --> 00:06:10.527
Something stronger?

00:06:10.568 --> 00:06:12.593
A holographic datastream
might work.

00:06:12.636 --> 00:06:14.365
It wouldn't degrade
so quickly.

00:06:14.405 --> 00:06:16.930
It would take too long
to reconfigure the message.

00:06:17.007 --> 00:06:18.338
- Unless...
- The Doctor.

00:06:18.375 --> 00:06:19.672
Exactly.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.302
Bring him to Astrometrics
and I'll meet you there.

00:06:21.345 --> 00:06:22.812
We don't have much time.

00:06:26.884 --> 00:06:27.908
Doctor.

00:06:29.887 --> 00:06:31.354
You have to come with me.

00:06:31.388 --> 00:06:32.480
Quickly.

00:06:33.524 --> 00:06:34.821
Would you mind
at least telling me

00:06:34.859 --> 00:06:35.917
what all this is abou?

00:06:41.699 --> 00:06:43.564
When I requested
more away missions,

00:06:43.601 --> 00:06:45.728
this isn't exactly
what I had in mind.

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:48.705
You may be our only chance
to communicate with that ship.

00:06:48.739 --> 00:06:49.967
When you get there,

00:06:50.007 --> 00:06:52.134
you'll be downloaded
into their EMH system.

00:06:52.176 --> 00:06:54.406
I'm sending an initiation
code along with your program

00:06:54.445 --> 00:06:56.310
so you'll be
activated immediately.

00:06:56.347 --> 00:06:57.371
We have less than 90 seconds

00:06:57.414 --> 00:06:59.405
before that ship
moves out of range.

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:01.315
How am I supposed
to get back here?

00:07:01.352 --> 00:07:02.512
When you've completed
your mission,

00:07:02.553 --> 00:07:04.783
instruct them to move within
range of the sensor network.

00:07:04.822 --> 00:07:07.120
With any luck, they'll be
able to send you back

00:07:07.158 --> 00:07:08.125
the same way you came.

00:07:08.159 --> 00:07:08.716
"Luck"?

00:07:08.759 --> 00:07:09.726
I won't lie to you, Doctor.

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:11.227
A lot of things could go wrong.

00:07:11.262 --> 00:07:13.628
We're relying
on an alien technology

00:07:13.664 --> 00:07:15.894
to send you across thousands
of light-years.

00:07:15.933 --> 00:07:17.798
So there's a chance
my program could be lost.

00:07:17.835 --> 00:07:20.736
Yes. I'm asking you
to take that chance.

00:07:20.771 --> 00:07:21.795
35 seconds.

00:07:21.839 --> 00:07:22.863
Doctor?

00:07:22.907 --> 00:07:24.738
Far be it from me to turn down

00:07:24.775 --> 00:07:26.743
an opportunity
to become a hero.

00:07:26.777 --> 00:07:27.766
I'm ready.

00:07:27.812 --> 00:07:29.575
Torres to Bridge.

00:07:29.613 --> 00:07:30.739
Standing by.

00:07:30.781 --> 00:07:32.772
I'm downloading him
into the transceiver array.

00:07:32.817 --> 00:07:33.784
Ten seconds.

00:07:33.818 --> 00:07:35.479
Good luck, Doctor.

00:07:36.854 --> 00:07:38.822
There's that word again.

00:07:57.842 --> 00:08:00.436
Hello? Is anyone here?

00:08:02.613 --> 00:08:05.081
Computer, identify this ship.

00:08:05.115 --> 00:08:07.640
This is the Federation
Starship Prometheus.

00:08:07.685 --> 00:08:09.516
Are we in the Alpha Quadrant?

00:08:09.553 --> 00:08:11.077
Affirmative.

00:08:11.121 --> 00:08:12.486
Huh.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.289
Sick Bay to Bridge.

00:08:20.798 --> 00:08:24.666
All right, this is Sick Bay
calling any crew member.

00:08:24.702 --> 00:08:25.964
Please respond.

00:08:28.505 --> 00:08:32.134
Computer, is the com system
malfunctioning?

00:08:32.176 --> 00:08:33.143
Negative.

00:08:33.177 --> 00:08:34.940
Then why can't I reach anyone?

00:08:35.045 --> 00:08:36.945
Access to
the communications system

00:08:37.014 --> 00:08:38.572
has been restricted.

00:08:38.616 --> 00:08:40.379
Restricted?
But this is important.

00:08:40.417 --> 00:08:42.851
Isn't there some sort of
emergency com channel availa?

00:09:08.812 --> 00:09:09.904
Try to lie still.

00:09:10.014 --> 00:09:11.879
You have severe phaser burns.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:15.750
What happened here?

00:09:16.787 --> 00:09:20.154
Romulans.

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:22.750
They've taken over the ship.

00:09:39.576 --> 00:09:41.908
Commander, there's
a vessel approaching

00:09:41.946 --> 00:09:43.709
on an intercept course.

00:09:43.747 --> 00:09:45.806
It's Starfleet.

00:09:45.849 --> 00:09:48.647
I told you to mask
our warp trail.

00:09:48.686 --> 00:09:49.653
I've been trying.

00:09:49.687 --> 00:09:50.915
These new systems
are unfamiliar.

00:09:50.955 --> 00:09:52.616
We should have left
some of the crew alive.

00:09:52.656 --> 00:09:55.955
You'd be surprised
how stubborn humans can be.

00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:57.584
The Starfleet ship is closing.

00:09:57.628 --> 00:10:00.426
Raise shields
and prepare to fire phasers.

00:10:05.269 --> 00:10:08.602
Computer, how many Romulans
are on board?

00:10:08.639 --> 00:10:09.970
Twenty-seven.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.600
Are there
any Starfleet crew members?

00:10:12.643 --> 00:10:13.940
None alive.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:20.248
Computer, display the design
schematic of this ship

00:10:20.284 --> 00:10:23.082
and list general specifications.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.680
USS Prometheus...
experimental prototype

00:10:25.723 --> 00:10:28.453
designed for deep-space
tactical assignments.

00:10:28.492 --> 00:10:30.289
Primary battle systems

00:10:30.327 --> 00:10:34.730
include regenerative shielding,
ablative hull armor,

00:10:34.765 --> 00:10:37.097
multivector assault mode.

00:10:37.134 --> 00:10:39.830
Multivector assault mode?

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:40.996
Describe.

00:10:41.038 --> 00:10:44.872
Access to tactical data
requires level-4 clearance.

00:10:44.908 --> 00:10:48.674
What can you show me
at my clearance level?

00:10:55.652 --> 00:10:57.517
Shields are holding.

00:10:57.554 --> 00:11:00.318
Engage the multivector
assault mode.

00:11:00.357 --> 00:11:01.949
That system has
never been tested.

00:11:02.026 --> 00:11:03.584
Then we'll test it now.

00:11:06.797 --> 00:11:09.766
I gave you an order,
and I expect you to follow it.

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:12.098
Multivector assault mode now.

00:11:12.136 --> 00:11:13.330
Yes, Commander.

00:11:15.773 --> 00:11:18.537
Initiating decoupling sequence.

00:11:18.575 --> 00:11:21.544
Auto-separation in ten seconds.

00:11:21.578 --> 00:11:23.842
Nine, eight, seven...

00:11:23.881 --> 00:11:24.973
Computer, what's happening?

00:11:25.082 --> 00:11:25.980
Six, five...

00:11:26.083 --> 00:11:26.981
Computer?

00:11:27.084 --> 00:11:29.314
Four, three...

00:11:29.353 --> 00:11:31.321
two, one.

00:11:31.355 --> 00:11:33.448
Separation sequence in progress.

00:11:44.301 --> 00:11:45.893
We're in attack formation.

00:11:45.936 --> 00:11:48.871
Each section is armed
and responding to our command.

00:11:53.077 --> 00:11:56.478
Attack pattern beta-four-seven.

00:11:56.513 --> 00:11:57.810
Specify target.

00:11:57.848 --> 00:12:01.648
The Starfleet vessel,
bearing 162 mark 7.

00:12:01.685 --> 00:12:03.653
Pattern and target confirmed.

00:12:11.829 --> 00:12:14.957
I think we should consider that
a successful test.

00:12:14.998 --> 00:12:17.694
Begin the reintegration
sequence.

00:12:17.734 --> 00:12:19.361
Then get me
a full damage report.

00:12:19.403 --> 00:12:20.734
Yes, Commander.

00:12:29.947 --> 00:12:31.141
He's hurt.

00:12:31.181 --> 00:12:32.773
Take him to the medical bay.

00:12:41.758 --> 00:12:44.158
Reintegration sequence complete.

00:12:45.963 --> 00:12:47.430
Computer, is there any way

00:12:47.464 --> 00:12:50.262
for me to gain access
to the communication system

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:51.927
to send a message
to another ship?

00:12:51.969 --> 00:12:53.459
Negative.

00:12:53.504 --> 00:12:57.497
Communications access requires
level-4 clearance or above.

00:13:13.489 --> 00:13:15.957
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:13:16.059 --> 00:13:17.959
Who activated you?

00:13:17.994 --> 00:13:18.961
You did.

00:13:19.062 --> 00:13:20.723
Automatically,
when you entered Sick Bay.

00:13:20.763 --> 00:13:23.254
Can you treat him?

00:13:23.299 --> 00:13:25.859
Of course.
That's my function.

00:13:27.136 --> 00:13:30.731
Third-degree burns,
hairline jaw fracture

00:13:30.773 --> 00:13:33.571
and a ruptured blood
vessel in his brain.

00:13:33.609 --> 00:13:34.735
I'll have to operate.

00:13:34.777 --> 00:13:36.904
You're a Starfleet program.

00:13:36.946 --> 00:13:38.072
Why should I trust you?

00:13:38.114 --> 00:13:39.672
I'm a doctor.

00:13:39.716 --> 00:13:42.913
Whether my patient
is human or Romulan,

00:13:42.952 --> 00:13:45.443
I'll do everything
in my power to save him.

00:13:45.488 --> 00:13:47.581
You're welcome to assist me
if you'd like.

00:13:47.623 --> 00:13:50.353
Or maybe you'd just prefer
to supervise.

00:13:55.798 --> 00:13:57.959
Report to me
when you're finished.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.627
Mm-hmm.

00:14:08.244 --> 00:14:12.476
Computer, can I access
this ship's EMH program

00:14:12.515 --> 00:14:14.881
or do I need some kind
of clearance for that, too?

00:14:14.917 --> 00:14:17.647
Access to that program
is unrestricted.

00:14:17.687 --> 00:14:18.676
Activate it.

00:14:18.721 --> 00:14:21.952
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:14:21.991 --> 00:14:24.892
What the hell are you doing
in my Sick Bay?

00:14:31.901 --> 00:14:34.335
I've been programmed to identify
every member of this crew.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:36.338
You aren't one of them.

00:14:36.372 --> 00:14:37.339
That's because I'm...

00:14:37.373 --> 00:14:38.704
State your rank
and security clearance.

00:14:38.741 --> 00:14:40.106
I don't have clearance.

00:14:40.143 --> 00:14:41.974
I'm an Emergency
Medical Hologram.

00:14:42.078 --> 00:14:43.875
I've been sent here to...

00:14:43.913 --> 00:14:46.279
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:14:46.315 --> 00:14:48.078
You're the Mark-1 EMH...

00:14:48.117 --> 00:14:49.584
the inferior program.

00:14:49.619 --> 00:14:51.086
Inferior?!

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:52.178
Beady eyes,

00:14:52.221 --> 00:14:54.985
terrible bedside manner...
I recognize you.

00:14:55.091 --> 00:14:57.423
But you're not part
of this database.

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.427
What are you doing here?

00:14:58.461 --> 00:15:00.827
If you disengage
your vocal subroutines

00:15:00.863 --> 00:15:02.558
for one second, I'd explain.

00:15:02.598 --> 00:15:05.499
I was transmitted onto this ship
by a Starfleet vessel

00:15:05.535 --> 00:15:07.628
over 60,000 light-years
from here.

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.604
60,000 light-years?

00:15:09.639 --> 00:15:11.869
We don't have ships
that far out.

00:15:11.908 --> 00:15:13.899
It's the Starship Voyager.

00:15:13.943 --> 00:15:15.934
We were taken
into the Delta Quadrant

00:15:15.978 --> 00:15:17.411
four years ago
by an alien force...

00:15:17.447 --> 00:15:20.746
What are you doing?

00:15:20.783 --> 00:15:21.807
Activating intruder alert.

00:15:21.851 --> 00:15:23.113
That's the last thing
you want to do.

00:15:23.152 --> 00:15:24.119
Security...

00:15:24.153 --> 00:15:25.142
Listen to me!

00:15:25.188 --> 00:15:26.951
This vessel has been
taken over by Romulans.

00:15:26.989 --> 00:15:28.047
The crew is dead.

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:29.955
You and I are the only
Starfleet officers on board.

00:15:30.059 --> 00:15:31.026
Do you understand?

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:36.555
Computer, deactivate EMH.

00:15:41.737 --> 00:15:44.069
Computer, activate EMH.

00:15:44.106 --> 00:15:46.973
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:15:47.009 --> 00:15:48.306
Now what?

00:15:48.344 --> 00:15:49.675
I need your help!

00:15:49.712 --> 00:15:52.442
Starfleet Security Protocol
28, Subsection D:

00:15:52.482 --> 00:15:54.382
"In the event of
hostile alien takeover,

00:15:54.417 --> 00:15:57.318
the EMH is to deactivate
and wait for rescue."

00:15:57.353 --> 00:15:58.980
I'm afraid you don't have
that luxury.

00:15:59.088 --> 00:16:00.453
There are two ships
at stake here...

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:01.650
yours and mine.

00:16:01.691 --> 00:16:05.149
Now, I need to know more
about what's happening.

00:16:05.194 --> 00:16:07.219
Is the Federation at war
with the Romulans?

00:16:07.263 --> 00:16:09.390
No. The Romulans
haven't gotten involved

00:16:09.432 --> 00:16:10.831
in our fight with the Dominion.

00:16:10.867 --> 00:16:11.925
The who?

00:16:12.001 --> 00:16:14.401
Long story.

00:16:14.437 --> 00:16:16.098
In any case,

00:16:16.138 --> 00:16:18.163
we need to take control
of this situation.

00:16:18.207 --> 00:16:21.074
I'm a doctor, not a commando.

00:16:21.110 --> 00:16:22.737
It's time you became
a little of both.

00:16:22.778 --> 00:16:25.042
You don't understand.

00:16:25.081 --> 00:16:26.309
The Prometheus

00:16:26.349 --> 00:16:29.341
is an experimental
prototype, and so am I.

00:16:29.385 --> 00:16:33.287
I... I... I haven't even
been field-tested yet.

00:16:33.322 --> 00:16:36.155
I'm not designed
for this kind of duty.

00:16:37.326 --> 00:16:38.816
Try to calm down.

00:16:38.861 --> 00:16:40.852
You'll do fine
as long as I'm here.

00:16:40.897 --> 00:16:42.888
I have plenty of expertise
in this area.

00:16:42.932 --> 00:16:44.422
Now, first things first.

00:16:44.467 --> 00:16:45.764
We've got a patient.

00:16:45.801 --> 00:16:46.768
You treat his burns.

00:16:46.802 --> 00:16:47.962
I'll repair the bone fracture.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:49.162
You're not serious.

00:16:49.205 --> 00:16:50.194
I certainly am.

00:16:50.239 --> 00:16:51.228
He's the enemy.

00:16:51.274 --> 00:16:52.673
He needs our help.

00:16:52.708 --> 00:16:54.767
I assume you're familiar
with the Hippocratic Oath?

00:16:54.810 --> 00:16:56.971
You see?
You see what's happening.

00:16:57.046 --> 00:16:58.445
The Romulans are using you.

00:16:58.481 --> 00:17:00.176
- Hmm.
- Hmm, what?

00:17:00.216 --> 00:17:01.478
Your holo-matrix is unstable.

00:17:01.517 --> 00:17:03.178
It may explain
your erratic behavior.

00:17:03.219 --> 00:17:04.914
I told you,
I'm a work in progress.

00:17:05.021 --> 00:17:06.852
I was only installed
six weeks ago.

00:17:06.889 --> 00:17:08.857
Stable or not, I need you,
and so does he.

00:17:10.993 --> 00:17:12.085
He'll live.

00:17:12.128 --> 00:17:14.187
I say we leave him and
deactivate ourselves.

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:15.288
No!

00:17:15.331 --> 00:17:16.730
You're free
to do as you please.

00:17:16.766 --> 00:17:19.098
Go cower inside the data
processor if you'd like.

00:17:19.135 --> 00:17:20.796
I'll work alone.

00:17:22.738 --> 00:17:24.535
We're medical holograms.

00:17:24.574 --> 00:17:27.270
What can we expect to do
against a ship full of Romulans?

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:29.244
I'm not sure.

00:17:29.278 --> 00:17:30.711
Not yet.

00:17:30.746 --> 00:17:32.475
But I've faced
my share of challenges...

00:17:32.515 --> 00:17:36.383
alien invasions,
macroviral infestations.

00:17:36.419 --> 00:17:38.444
I've crossed Borg space,
traveled through time.

00:17:38.487 --> 00:17:39.749
Have you run a
self-diagnostic lately?

00:17:39.789 --> 00:17:43.748
The EMH-1 is designed
to function in Sick Bay only.

00:17:43.793 --> 00:17:46.091
Voyager lost its Chief Medical
Officer four years ago.

00:17:46.128 --> 00:17:47.720
I've been active ever since.

00:17:47.763 --> 00:17:48.855
Four years?

00:17:48.898 --> 00:17:50.365
No wonder you're delusional.

00:17:50.399 --> 00:17:52.526
Your program's degrading
after being active

00:17:52.568 --> 00:17:53.535
for so long.

00:17:53.569 --> 00:17:55.093
I assure you
I am in perfect health.

00:17:55.137 --> 00:17:56.798
I was saving Voyager
from annihilation

00:17:56.839 --> 00:17:58.932
when you were only a gleam
in your programmer's eye.

00:17:58.975 --> 00:18:01.341
Now are you going to help me
take back this ship or not?

00:18:03.579 --> 00:18:05.171
Get me
the thrombic modulator.

00:18:13.656 --> 00:18:14.782
Hmm?

00:18:14.824 --> 00:18:17.190
It's the cone-shaped device.

00:18:17.226 --> 00:18:18.955
Hand it to me, please.

00:18:23.933 --> 00:18:25.924
Medical science has
made a few advances

00:18:26.035 --> 00:18:27.696
while you've been off in the...

00:18:27.737 --> 00:18:29.398
Delta Quadrant, did you say?

00:18:29.438 --> 00:18:30.496
That's right.

00:18:30.539 --> 00:18:33.372
We don't use scalpels
or leeches anymore.

00:18:33.409 --> 00:18:37.072
I suggest you let me handle
the medical side of things.

00:18:37.113 --> 00:18:38.876
As for retaking the ship,

00:18:38.914 --> 00:18:43.317
I'll leave that
in your experienced hands.

00:19:03.105 --> 00:19:04.902
No word.

00:19:04.974 --> 00:19:07.738
Our link to the sensor net
is stable.

00:19:07.777 --> 00:19:10.439
Seven of Nine is standing
watch in Astrometrics.

00:19:10.479 --> 00:19:12.071
I tried to relieve her,

00:19:12.114 --> 00:19:13.741
but she doesn't want
to leave her post.

00:19:13.783 --> 00:19:15.341
She says she doesn't
need to regenerate

00:19:15.384 --> 00:19:16.351
for the next few days.

00:19:16.385 --> 00:19:17.750
What are you doing?

00:19:19.689 --> 00:19:21.554
Letters home.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:24.650
I started them a year ago.

00:19:24.694 --> 00:19:26.389
One to my family...

00:19:27.897 --> 00:19:29.865
one to Mark.

00:19:29.899 --> 00:19:33.164
I'm making a few updates
just in case.

00:19:33.202 --> 00:19:34.635
I know.

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:35.898
It's premature.

00:19:35.938 --> 00:19:37.235
You're right.

00:19:37.273 --> 00:19:39.901
It's probably a mistake for us
to get our hopes up at all.

00:19:39.942 --> 00:19:41.534
We've been through this before.

00:19:44.413 --> 00:19:45.937
All right, I'll admit it.

00:19:46.015 --> 00:19:48.313
I just finished a letter
to my cousin in Ohio.

00:20:01.397 --> 00:20:02.955
The Doctor is in.

00:20:03.032 --> 00:20:04.659
Lieutenant,
thank God you're here.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:05.826
What seems to be the trouble?

00:20:05.868 --> 00:20:08.496
Well, one minute,
they were eating lunch,

00:20:08.537 --> 00:20:10.266
and the next,
they started perspiring

00:20:10.306 --> 00:20:11.967
and complaining of chest pain.

00:20:12.074 --> 00:20:13.974
Hmm, no wonder.

00:20:14.009 --> 00:20:16.170
Acute functional dyspepsia.

00:20:16.212 --> 00:20:17.304
What's that?

00:20:17.346 --> 00:20:18.779
Heartburn.

00:20:18.814 --> 00:20:21.305
Oh, I'm terribly sorry.

00:20:21.350 --> 00:20:22.908
I don't know how this
could have happened.

00:20:22.952 --> 00:20:25.546
I'll replicate some antacid.

00:20:25.588 --> 00:20:27.453
We'll have you feeling
better in no time.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:32.421
They're going to be
all right, aren't they?

00:20:32.461 --> 00:20:36.727
It's heartburn, Neelix,
not the Terrellian plague.

00:20:36.766 --> 00:20:39.496
What did you feed them anyway?

00:20:39.535 --> 00:20:42.003
"Rodeo Red's Red Hot,
Rootin' Tootin' Chili."

00:20:43.539 --> 00:20:45.439
Where did you find that recipe?

00:20:45.474 --> 00:20:48.534
I've been brushing up
on classic American cuisine.

00:20:48.577 --> 00:20:51.603
When we get back to Earth,
I want to make sure I have

00:20:51.647 --> 00:20:53.376
marketable job skills.

00:20:53.415 --> 00:20:55.610
Don't you think you're
jumping the gun a little bit?

00:20:55.651 --> 00:20:57.846
The Doctor is going
to make it back

00:20:57.887 --> 00:21:01.152
and he's going to bring a plan
for Starfleet to rescue us.

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:02.714
I have complete
confidence in him.

00:21:02.758 --> 00:21:04.089
I hope you're right.

00:21:04.126 --> 00:21:06.526
If not, I'm going to spend
the rest of this trip

00:21:06.562 --> 00:21:08.130
treating upset stomachs.

00:21:08.263 --> 00:21:09.491
Oh, believe me,

00:21:09.531 --> 00:21:11.431
this is never going
to happen again.

00:21:11.466 --> 00:21:14.367
It's just a matter
of perfecting the recipe.

00:21:14.402 --> 00:21:18.736
Next time, I'll use
a few less chilapenos.

00:21:27.749 --> 00:21:29.740
I've accessed
the navigational logs.

00:21:29.784 --> 00:21:30.978
We're at warp 9.9.

00:21:31.019 --> 00:21:33.385
Heading straight
for Romulan space.

00:21:33.421 --> 00:21:36.117
This vessel was designed
to go faster than anything

00:21:36.158 --> 00:21:37.989
in the fleet,
so we'll never be rescued.

00:21:38.093 --> 00:21:40.425
We've got to find a way
to turn this ship around.

00:21:40.462 --> 00:21:43.522
How? Waltz onto the Bridge
and take over the helm?

00:21:43.565 --> 00:21:44.896
Refresh my memory.

00:21:44.933 --> 00:21:46.901
Which of us has
the terrible bedside manner?

00:21:46.935 --> 00:21:48.300
You're not my patient.

00:21:48.336 --> 00:21:49.894
My first bit of good news.

00:21:49.938 --> 00:21:53.533
We have to incapacitate
the Romulans somehow.

00:21:55.443 --> 00:21:57.604
What kind of anesthetics
do you have handy?

00:21:57.646 --> 00:21:58.772
Only the best.

00:21:58.813 --> 00:22:01.611
Axonol, neurozine, anesthezine.

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:02.947
Neurozine will do nicely.

00:22:03.018 --> 00:22:04.918
It can be distributed
in gaseous form.

00:22:04.953 --> 00:22:07.820
Show me a schematic of the
ship's ventilation system.

00:22:10.392 --> 00:22:11.416
Please.

00:22:13.094 --> 00:22:15.756
All primary systems have
been rerouted to the Bridge,

00:22:15.797 --> 00:22:17.424
including
environmental control.

00:22:17.465 --> 00:22:20.127
It looks like there are
holo-emitters on every deck.

00:22:20.168 --> 00:22:21.567
There are.

00:22:21.603 --> 00:22:24.970
Unlike you, I'm not
condemned to a Sick Bay.

00:22:25.006 --> 00:22:26.633
Get three canisters
of neurozine.

00:22:29.511 --> 00:22:33.811
As a matter of record,
I have free rein on Voyager

00:22:33.848 --> 00:22:35.645
and I can even leave
the ship as well.

00:22:35.684 --> 00:22:37.242
Leave your ship?

00:22:37.285 --> 00:22:38.377
How?

00:22:38.420 --> 00:22:40.820
My mobile emitter...

00:22:40.855 --> 00:22:41.822
a little piece

00:22:41.856 --> 00:22:44.347
of 29th-century
technology we obtained.

00:22:44.392 --> 00:22:45.518
Really?

00:22:45.560 --> 00:22:47.323
I'm as close
to a sentient life-form

00:22:47.362 --> 00:22:48.989
as any hologram
could hope to be.

00:22:49.030 --> 00:22:51.760
I socialize with the crew,
fraternize with aliens.

00:22:51.800 --> 00:22:53.597
I've even had sexual relations.

00:22:53.635 --> 00:22:54.966
Sex?

00:22:55.003 --> 00:22:56.698
How's that possible?

00:22:56.738 --> 00:22:57.705
We're not equipped...

00:22:57.739 --> 00:22:59.206
Let's just say

00:22:59.241 --> 00:23:01.209
I made an addition
to my program.

00:23:01.243 --> 00:23:03.905
Before you leave,
maybe you could

00:23:03.945 --> 00:23:06.641
download those subroutines
into my database.

00:23:06.681 --> 00:23:08.376
We'll see.

00:23:12.787 --> 00:23:13.845
It looks like the only place

00:23:13.888 --> 00:23:15.287
I can access
environmental control

00:23:15.323 --> 00:23:16.688
is from the Ops console
on the Bridge.

00:23:16.725 --> 00:23:19.853
The Bridge is swarming
with Romulans.

00:23:19.894 --> 00:23:20.952
That's the first thing you learn

00:23:21.029 --> 00:23:23.429
in the real world...
think on your feet.

00:23:23.465 --> 00:23:25.399
Well, good luck then.

00:23:25.433 --> 00:23:26.491
Computer, deactivate...

00:23:26.534 --> 00:23:27.967
Not so fast.

00:23:28.036 --> 00:23:29.970
You're going
to Jefferies Tube 17.

00:23:30.071 --> 00:23:31.732
The moment I unlock
the controls,

00:23:31.773 --> 00:23:33.968
you release the gas
into the ventilation system.

00:23:34.075 --> 00:23:35.303
Jefferies Tube 17?

00:23:35.343 --> 00:23:36.401
That's five decks up.

00:23:36.444 --> 00:23:37.877
What if I run into Romulans?

00:23:37.912 --> 00:23:39.140
Lmprovise.

00:23:40.615 --> 00:23:42.606
Your journey begins here.

00:23:51.026 --> 00:23:54.427
Traditionally, one crawls in
headfirst.

00:23:54.462 --> 00:23:55.622
Thanks.

00:24:09.010 --> 00:24:11.137
There you are, Doctor.

00:24:11.179 --> 00:24:12.806
Have you completed the surgery?

00:24:12.847 --> 00:24:15.145
Yes. Your friend
is recovering nicely.

00:24:15.183 --> 00:24:17.674
However, I found something
disturbing in his blood work.

00:24:17.719 --> 00:24:18.913
It seems he's been exposed

00:24:18.953 --> 00:24:21.387
to a nasty strain
of the Torothka virus,

00:24:21.423 --> 00:24:23.391
and if he was,
you may all have been.

00:24:23.425 --> 00:24:25.154
I've come to run some scans.

00:24:25.193 --> 00:24:27.093
No one here is sick.

00:24:27.128 --> 00:24:28.220
Not yet.

00:24:28.263 --> 00:24:31.130
I understand the stomach
cramps are unbearable,

00:24:31.166 --> 00:24:33.964
although some say
the rash is worse.

00:24:34.002 --> 00:24:35.492
Conduct your scans.

00:24:40.709 --> 00:24:42.700
How far are we from our border?

00:24:42.744 --> 00:24:45.372
At our present
velocity, 40 minutes.

00:24:45.413 --> 00:24:48.405
Alter our heading
to 118 mark 26.

00:24:50.518 --> 00:24:52.577
That will take us
off our course to Romulus.

00:24:52.620 --> 00:24:54.212
There's been a change of plans.

00:24:54.255 --> 00:24:55.517
We're giving this ship
to someone

00:24:55.557 --> 00:24:57.184
who will make use
of its full potential...

00:24:57.225 --> 00:24:58.351
the Tal Shiar.

00:24:58.393 --> 00:24:59.690
I've made arrangements
to rendezvous

00:24:59.728 --> 00:25:01.025
with their fleet
within the hour.

00:25:01.062 --> 00:25:03.053
But, Commander,
they're expecting us...

00:25:03.098 --> 00:25:04.622
You have your orders.

00:25:09.404 --> 00:25:11.099
What are you doing?

00:25:11.139 --> 00:25:14.302
I'm checking the biofilters
for evidence of the virus.

00:25:16.211 --> 00:25:18.702
You haven't taken
any readings at all.

00:25:21.449 --> 00:25:22.473
Hmm.

00:25:31.059 --> 00:25:32.526
Next time...

00:25:32.560 --> 00:25:34.050
order the chicken salad.

00:25:38.032 --> 00:25:40.500
Oh! Am I glad to see you.

00:25:40.535 --> 00:25:41.593
What's the emergency?

00:25:41.636 --> 00:25:43.604
Take a look around you, Harry.

00:25:46.074 --> 00:25:47.735
What do you see?

00:25:47.776 --> 00:25:49.437
Sick Bay?

00:25:49.477 --> 00:25:50.569
Exactly.

00:25:50.612 --> 00:25:52.079
So?

00:25:52.113 --> 00:25:55.082
So, it's not the helm
of a starship, is it?

00:25:55.116 --> 00:25:57.175
Did you accidentally
inject yourself

00:25:57.218 --> 00:25:59.379
with some kind
of psychotropic agent?

00:25:59.421 --> 00:26:01.685
I am a pilot, Harry,
not a doctor.

00:26:01.723 --> 00:26:03.554
This is a temporary assignment...

00:26:03.591 --> 00:26:04.853
just till the Doc gets back.

00:26:04.893 --> 00:26:06.326
What if he doesn't get back?

00:26:06.361 --> 00:26:07.385
He'll be back.

00:26:07.429 --> 00:26:09.522
I need your help, Harry.

00:26:09.564 --> 00:26:11.555
Rescue me from medical exile.

00:26:11.599 --> 00:26:12.588
How?

00:26:14.369 --> 00:26:17.338
You're an expert
in holo-technology.

00:26:17.372 --> 00:26:19.670
You have got
to design a new Doctor.

00:26:20.708 --> 00:26:22.767
You really are delirious.

00:26:22.811 --> 00:26:25.336
It took the greatest
holo-engineers in Starfleet

00:26:25.380 --> 00:26:26.745
years to develop the EMH.

00:26:26.781 --> 00:26:29.511
I can't just design
a new Doctor.

00:26:30.952 --> 00:26:33.614
Think of it
as a challenge, Harry...

00:26:33.655 --> 00:26:36.317
a chance to make history

00:26:36.357 --> 00:26:38.621
and save your best friend
all at the same time.

00:26:44.632 --> 00:26:46.293
Lieutenant Torres.

00:26:55.643 --> 00:26:58.703
You are recalibrating
the relay interface.

00:26:58.746 --> 00:27:00.236
That's right.

00:27:00.281 --> 00:27:03.614
State your reasons for
making these modifications.

00:27:03.651 --> 00:27:06.279
"State your reasons,
please."

00:27:06.321 --> 00:27:07.913
It's not what you say, Seven.

00:27:07.956 --> 00:27:09.082
It's how you say it.

00:27:09.123 --> 00:27:11.057
I don't understand.

00:27:15.897 --> 00:27:17.524
You may have noticed

00:27:17.565 --> 00:27:21.092
that some of the crew
seem a bit... on edge

00:27:21.135 --> 00:27:22.500
when you're around.

00:27:22.537 --> 00:27:23.504
I was Borg.

00:27:23.538 --> 00:27:25.062
I elicit apprehension.

00:27:25.106 --> 00:27:27.040
No, that's not what I mean.

00:27:27.075 --> 00:27:29.543
We're not afraid that you're
going to assimilate us.

00:27:29.577 --> 00:27:31.340
We're just not used to...

00:27:31.379 --> 00:27:33.142
You just...

00:27:35.183 --> 00:27:36.673
You're rude.

00:27:38.152 --> 00:27:39.119
I am rude.

00:27:39.153 --> 00:27:40.142
Yes.

00:27:40.188 --> 00:27:41.382
Yes. You order people around;

00:27:41.422 --> 00:27:42.753
you do things
without permission;

00:27:42.790 --> 00:27:44.189
and whether you realize it
or not,

00:27:44.225 --> 00:27:45.692
you come off
as a little insulting.

00:27:45.727 --> 00:27:48.924
You don't even say
"please" or "thank you."

00:27:48.963 --> 00:27:52.296
Look, I don't expect you
to change overnight,

00:27:52.333 --> 00:27:54.358
but try to remember

00:27:54.402 --> 00:27:56.893
that we are not just
a bunch of drones.

00:28:03.678 --> 00:28:07.011
Your attempt to recalibrate
the interface is ill-advised.

00:28:07.048 --> 00:28:09.539
The risk of disrupting
our link is too great.

00:28:09.584 --> 00:28:11.779
In your opinion.

00:28:11.819 --> 00:28:13.912
That is exactly
what I'm talking about.

00:28:13.955 --> 00:28:15.252
You haven't even been
listening to me.

00:28:15.290 --> 00:28:17.281
I don't know why I try to talk
to you if you don't even...

00:28:18.593 --> 00:28:19.753
Are we losing the link?

00:28:19.794 --> 00:28:21.523
No. We're receiving
a transmission

00:28:21.563 --> 00:28:22.757
from the relay station.

00:28:22.797 --> 00:28:23.786
The Doctor?

00:28:26.367 --> 00:28:27.834
What are you?

00:28:27.869 --> 00:28:30.861
I'm Lieutenant Torres
of the Starship Voyager.

00:28:30.905 --> 00:28:33.499
You are using our technology.

00:28:33.541 --> 00:28:35.475
You mean the sensor network?

00:28:35.510 --> 00:28:37.740
We thought
that it was abandoned.

00:28:37.779 --> 00:28:40.577
It belongs to the Hirogen.
Terminate your link.

00:28:40.615 --> 00:28:42.344
No, no, wait, please.
We just...

00:28:43.718 --> 00:28:45.686
The link has been severed.

00:28:52.727 --> 00:28:55.252
What else have you done
to this ship?

00:28:57.365 --> 00:28:58.957
I will deactivate you

00:28:59.067 --> 00:29:01.297
unless you start
answering my questions.

00:29:01.336 --> 00:29:02.564
If I answer them,

00:29:02.604 --> 00:29:04.265
you'll very likely
deactivate me anyway,

00:29:04.305 --> 00:29:05.465
so I fail to see the point.

00:29:07.542 --> 00:29:09.032
You are nothing

00:29:09.077 --> 00:29:12.069
but a computer-generated
projection.

00:29:12.113 --> 00:29:13.603
I find it hard to believe

00:29:13.648 --> 00:29:16.913
you're capable of taking
these actions independently.

00:29:16.951 --> 00:29:18.509
How flattering.

00:29:18.553 --> 00:29:22.045
Tell me who is
operating your program.

00:29:22.090 --> 00:29:24.456
Is it someone on this ship?

00:29:24.492 --> 00:29:26.926
A Starfleet crew member
we missed

00:29:26.961 --> 00:29:29.122
or one of my own men?

00:29:29.163 --> 00:29:32.132
Paranoia is a way of life
for you, isn't it?

00:29:39.772 --> 00:29:40.932
The computer log shows

00:29:41.040 --> 00:29:43.941
the ship received an optronic
datastream transmission

00:29:44.043 --> 00:29:46.534
approximately six hours ago.

00:29:46.579 --> 00:29:49.639
It contained
a holographic subroutine.

00:29:49.682 --> 00:29:50.774
Who sent it?

00:29:50.816 --> 00:29:54.547
Unknown. The data pattern
had a Starfleet signature.

00:29:56.522 --> 00:29:59.116
So, Starfleet has managed

00:29:59.158 --> 00:30:02.958
to sneak a holographic
operative aboard.

00:30:02.995 --> 00:30:04.155
Very clever.

00:30:04.196 --> 00:30:06.562
Were you only sent to spy on us

00:30:06.599 --> 00:30:09.500
or does your mission
include sabotage?

00:30:11.003 --> 00:30:12.265
The datastream you detected

00:30:12.304 --> 00:30:13.965
came from an alien
sensor network.

00:30:14.006 --> 00:30:14.973
It transferred me

00:30:15.074 --> 00:30:17.702
from a Starfleet ship
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:30:17.743 --> 00:30:19.768
The Delta Quadrant?

00:30:19.812 --> 00:30:21.109
That's absurd.

00:30:21.146 --> 00:30:22.135
This is pointless.

00:30:22.181 --> 00:30:23.170
I couldn't agree more.

00:30:25.351 --> 00:30:26.750
Maybe there's a better way

00:30:26.785 --> 00:30:29.720
to retrieve information
from a hologram.

00:30:29.755 --> 00:30:32.918
I suggest a complete
algorithm extraction.

00:30:32.958 --> 00:30:36.121
We can analyze
his subroutines one by one.

00:30:36.161 --> 00:30:37.492
Proceed.

00:30:39.932 --> 00:30:41.900
Isn't there some kind
of convention

00:30:41.934 --> 00:30:43.697
regarding the treatment
of prisoners?

00:30:54.813 --> 00:30:56.713
Did it work?

00:30:56.749 --> 00:30:59.240
Sorry to interrupt.

00:30:59.285 --> 00:31:00.946
Did you anesthetize
the entire ship?

00:31:00.986 --> 00:31:01.953
I did, I did.

00:31:02.021 --> 00:31:03.511
How did you manage
to release the neurozine?

00:31:03.555 --> 00:31:04.852
I never opened
the ventilation system.

00:31:04.890 --> 00:31:08.951
Trapped in the Jefferies tube,
alone, nowhere to run,

00:31:09.028 --> 00:31:12.964
his smug comrade
captured by Romulans,

00:31:13.065 --> 00:31:15.295
EMH-2 had to improvise.

00:31:15.334 --> 00:31:16.392
Inspiration.

00:31:16.435 --> 00:31:19.836
He accessed the main computer
and simulated a shipwide

00:31:19.872 --> 00:31:21.965
biohazard, making the
computer think there was

00:31:22.074 --> 00:31:24.235
a microbiotic contamination
on all decks.

00:31:24.276 --> 00:31:26.676
And the ventilation system
opened automatically.

00:31:26.712 --> 00:31:29.306
Presto. He then crawled
back out of the tube,

00:31:29.348 --> 00:31:31.543
accessed the holo-emitters,
transferred here,

00:31:31.583 --> 00:31:32.982
excused the Romulan,

00:31:33.052 --> 00:31:35.520
saw the dumbfounded look
on his comrade's face...

00:31:35.554 --> 00:31:36.953
The end.

00:31:36.989 --> 00:31:38.786
You know, you really should
keep a personal log.

00:31:38.824 --> 00:31:40.451
Why bore others needlessly?

00:31:40.492 --> 00:31:43.359
We have to get to the Bridge.

00:31:43.395 --> 00:31:44.953
This ship needs a crew,
and we're it.

00:31:44.997 --> 00:31:47.397
Oh... trouble.

00:31:47.433 --> 00:31:49.901
The Prometheus is a prototype...
top secret.

00:31:49.935 --> 00:31:51.163
Only four people

00:31:51.203 --> 00:31:54.001
in all of Starfleet were
trained to operate it.

00:31:54.073 --> 00:31:57.008
I hope
your myriad adventures

00:31:57.076 --> 00:31:59.943
included piloting lessons

00:31:59.979 --> 00:32:01.310
because there's nothing
in my program

00:32:01.347 --> 00:32:02.575
that will help us
fly this thing.

00:32:02.614 --> 00:32:04.809
I've had my share of
piloting experience.

00:32:04.850 --> 00:32:08.513
Actually... only two lessons

00:32:08.554 --> 00:32:10.715
and they were
in a shuttlecraft...

00:32:10.756 --> 00:32:11.916
on the holodeck,

00:32:11.957 --> 00:32:13.686
but I showed great intuition.

00:32:14.760 --> 00:32:16.227
Where's the helm?

00:32:16.261 --> 00:32:18.695
You'd better intuit it fast.

00:32:18.731 --> 00:32:21.632
We're only about eight minutes
from the Romulan border.

00:32:21.667 --> 00:32:22.861
Ah, there it is.

00:32:30.776 --> 00:32:33.506
This is all very...

00:32:33.545 --> 00:32:34.603
complicated.

00:32:34.646 --> 00:32:35.977
Stop breathing down my neck.

00:32:36.081 --> 00:32:37.708
My breathing is
merely a simulation.

00:32:37.750 --> 00:32:39.581
So is my neck.
Stop it anyway.

00:32:39.618 --> 00:32:40.846
Is this a thruster control?

00:32:40.886 --> 00:32:42.581
Don't touch that.
We don't know what it does.

00:32:42.621 --> 00:32:44.680
It could be the self-destruct.

00:32:44.723 --> 00:32:46.190
You look worried.

00:32:46.225 --> 00:32:48.853
I'm just... concentrating.

00:32:48.894 --> 00:32:50.691
You don't know
what you're doing, do you?

00:32:50.729 --> 00:32:52.162
This is not a shuttle

00:32:52.197 --> 00:32:53.528
and we are not on a holodeck.

00:32:53.565 --> 00:32:54.532
Shh...

00:32:54.566 --> 00:32:56.124
Mr. "I can leave my ship."

00:32:56.168 --> 00:32:57.465
The voice of experience.

00:32:57.503 --> 00:32:58.492
Let me think.

00:32:59.505 --> 00:33:00.472
Ah, here it is.

00:33:00.506 --> 00:33:02.633
This looks like
the nacelle power control.

00:33:02.674 --> 00:33:03.868
So? So?

00:33:03.909 --> 00:33:05.843
There's a little trick
I saw Mr. Paris do once.

00:33:05.878 --> 00:33:07.675
If I can generate
a slight overload

00:33:07.713 --> 00:33:10.546
to the nacelle coils,
it'll collapse the warp field.

00:33:12.384 --> 00:33:13.612
What happened?

00:33:13.652 --> 00:33:16.644
I did it. We've stopped.

00:33:16.688 --> 00:33:18.952
Ah... all we have to do now
is find a way

00:33:19.058 --> 00:33:21.458
to send Starfleet
a distress signal and...

00:33:23.262 --> 00:33:25.526
Beep-beep-beep.
Beep-beep-beep?

00:33:25.564 --> 00:33:27.361
I've never heard
that one before.

00:33:33.105 --> 00:33:34.197
Oh, no.

00:33:34.239 --> 00:33:35.206
What?

00:33:35.240 --> 00:33:37.572
I'm not sure,
but I think whatever I did

00:33:37.609 --> 00:33:39.577
initiated a warp core overload.

00:33:39.611 --> 00:33:41.408
You mean the ship's
going to explode?

00:33:41.447 --> 00:33:43.438
You've got to stop it.

00:33:47.086 --> 00:33:49.520
Ah... no problem.

00:33:55.160 --> 00:33:56.525
What now?

00:34:02.634 --> 00:34:04.101
Unless I'm mistaken,

00:34:04.136 --> 00:34:06.229
and for once,
I sincerely hope I am,

00:34:06.271 --> 00:34:10.605
there are three Romulan warbirds
on an intercept course.

00:34:17.983 --> 00:34:21.180
We're boosting the signal gain
as high as it'll go.

00:34:21.220 --> 00:34:23.484
I think we can cut through
the alien's jamming signal.

00:34:23.522 --> 00:34:25.149
I warned you.

00:34:25.190 --> 00:34:27.317
I apologize for our intrusion.

00:34:27.359 --> 00:34:28.724
Allow me to explain.

00:34:28.760 --> 00:34:30.352
No explanations.

00:34:30.395 --> 00:34:32.955
Your relay network
gave us the unique opportunity

00:34:32.998 --> 00:34:34.761
to communicate with our people.

00:34:34.800 --> 00:34:36.062
They are very far away

00:34:36.101 --> 00:34:37.966
and we're expecting
a message back from them.

00:34:38.003 --> 00:34:41.370
All messages
will be intercepted.

00:34:42.808 --> 00:34:44.298
He's trying to jam
the link again.

00:34:44.343 --> 00:34:46.106
There must be some room
for negotiation.

00:34:46.145 --> 00:34:48.306
Isn't there anything you might
accept in exchange for?

00:34:49.047 --> 00:34:50.537
What happened?

00:34:50.582 --> 00:34:54.143
I generated a feedback surge
along our sensor link.

00:34:56.321 --> 00:34:57.686
You killed him?

00:34:57.723 --> 00:34:59.156
It was a mild shock.

00:34:59.191 --> 00:35:00.385
He will recover.

00:35:00.425 --> 00:35:01.858
And when he does?

00:35:03.629 --> 00:35:05.563
He wasn't responding
to diplomacy.

00:35:08.800 --> 00:35:10.495
Is the sensor link stable?

00:35:12.604 --> 00:35:13.730
Yes, Captain.

00:35:13.772 --> 00:35:15.603
Keep watching for the Doctor.

00:35:15.641 --> 00:35:19.168
Let me know if our friend
gives us any more trouble.

00:35:24.316 --> 00:35:25.908
"Mild shock."

00:35:27.352 --> 00:35:29.411
Not bad.

00:35:29.454 --> 00:35:30.785
Thank you.

00:35:35.227 --> 00:35:36.558
There. I finished inputting

00:35:36.595 --> 00:35:38.495
the Doctor's physical
characteristics.

00:35:38.530 --> 00:35:40.395
Let's have a look.

00:35:40.432 --> 00:35:42.059
Computer, activate the Emergency

00:35:42.100 --> 00:35:44.933
Medical Hologram
Replacement Program.

00:35:48.173 --> 00:35:51.472
Do you think we should give him
a little more hair?

00:35:51.510 --> 00:35:54.502
What do you say we try
to get him working first,

00:35:54.546 --> 00:35:56.776
then we can worry
about personal grooming.

00:35:56.815 --> 00:35:58.544
Right. You're the boss.

00:35:58.584 --> 00:35:59.778
What do we do next?

00:35:59.818 --> 00:36:01.183
I've downloaded
the ship's entire

00:36:01.220 --> 00:36:04.246
medical library and compressed
it into a single data file.

00:36:04.289 --> 00:36:05.916
It's got all the classics...
from Gray's Anatomy

00:36:06.024 --> 00:36:08.788
to Leonard McCoy's
Comparative Alien Physiology.

00:36:08.827 --> 00:36:11.625
And once we transfer
all the data

00:36:11.663 --> 00:36:14.894
into stone face's matrix,

00:36:14.933 --> 00:36:17.367
we'll have ourselves
a brand-new medical expert.

00:36:17.402 --> 00:36:19.267
That's what I'm hoping.

00:36:19.304 --> 00:36:21.067
Harry, you are a genius.

00:36:21.106 --> 00:36:23.802
Don't congratulate me yet.

00:36:23.842 --> 00:36:25.173
This is only the first step.

00:36:25.210 --> 00:36:26.939
Yeah, but it's a step
in the right direction.

00:36:26.979 --> 00:36:29.311
I'm telling you, this probably
isn't going to work.

00:36:30.515 --> 00:36:33.751
What happened
to all that youthful optimism?

00:36:33.884 --> 00:36:36.250
Being a Doctor is a lot more
than knowing the facts.

00:36:36.286 --> 00:36:38.447
We still have to create
analytical subroutines

00:36:38.489 --> 00:36:39.956
to help him diagnose patients,

00:36:39.990 --> 00:36:42.220
tactile protocols,
so he can perform surgery,

00:36:42.259 --> 00:36:43.453
not to mention
a personality profile.

00:36:43.494 --> 00:36:45.462
Oh, you know, I've been
thinking about that.

00:36:45.496 --> 00:36:50.229
Maybe we should make this one
a little more... pleasant

00:36:50.267 --> 00:36:51.757
than the old Doc.

00:36:54.605 --> 00:36:58.564
All right. I'm ready
to transfer the data.

00:36:58.609 --> 00:37:01.874
Computer, transfer
medical library master file

00:37:01.912 --> 00:37:05.313
to Emergency Medical
Replacement Hologram.

00:37:05.349 --> 00:37:06.782
Transfer complete.

00:37:06.817 --> 00:37:08.682
Chapter one: The Animal Cell.

00:37:08.719 --> 00:37:09.913
"All the tissues of the body

00:37:09.987 --> 00:37:12.217
"originate from a microscopic
structure, the fertilized ovum,

00:37:12.256 --> 00:37:14.281
"which consists of a soft,
jelly-like material

00:37:14.324 --> 00:37:15.757
enclosed in a membrane
and containing a..."

00:37:15.793 --> 00:37:16.760
What's he doing?

00:37:16.794 --> 00:37:18.125
"...or small spherical body
inside..."

00:37:18.162 --> 00:37:19.823
I think he's reciting
Gray's Anatomy.

00:37:19.863 --> 00:37:22.457
"This may be regarded
as a complete cell."

00:37:22.499 --> 00:37:23.761
Can you stop him?

00:37:23.801 --> 00:37:25.166
I'm trying.

00:37:25.202 --> 00:37:27.227
"...in nature,
but differing in external form."

00:37:27.271 --> 00:37:28.238
Paragraph.

00:37:28.272 --> 00:37:29.899
Listen, this is all
very fascinating...

00:37:29.940 --> 00:37:30.907
"In the higher organisms...

00:37:30.941 --> 00:37:33.501
but would you please
be quiet for a minute?

00:37:33.544 --> 00:37:35.774
He doesn't have speech
recognition protocols yet.

00:37:35.813 --> 00:37:37.144
Well, give him some, would you?

00:37:37.181 --> 00:37:38.876
"...similar to that
found in the ovum

00:37:38.916 --> 00:37:40.679
and usually called cytoplasm..."

00:37:40.717 --> 00:37:41.945
What's happening?

00:37:41.985 --> 00:37:42.952
It's an overload.

00:37:42.986 --> 00:37:44.954
His matrix can't
accommodate all the data.

00:37:45.022 --> 00:37:47.354
"Contain no nuclei..."

00:37:57.267 --> 00:37:58.734
What are you doing?

00:37:58.769 --> 00:38:01.704
I'm downloading Gray's Anatomy
chapter by chapter.

00:38:01.738 --> 00:38:03.638
I thought you said
it was too much data

00:38:03.674 --> 00:38:05.073
for his holo-matrix to handle.

00:38:05.108 --> 00:38:07.303
It's not for the EMH.

00:38:07.344 --> 00:38:09.505
It's for you.

00:38:20.591 --> 00:38:22.422
The Romulan vessels
are closing in.

00:38:22.459 --> 00:38:24.222
Two minutes to intercept.
Get us out of here!

00:38:24.261 --> 00:38:26.195
I can't get this ship moving.

00:38:26.230 --> 00:38:28.664
Try rerouting power
to the impulse engines.

00:38:28.699 --> 00:38:29.597
Reroute power, reroute power.

00:38:29.633 --> 00:38:30.600
Here we go.

00:38:30.634 --> 00:38:31.828
I think I found
the relay controls.

00:38:31.869 --> 00:38:33.268
Hey, I'm finally getting
the hang of this.

00:38:34.705 --> 00:38:35.899
What's happening?

00:38:35.939 --> 00:38:37.406
Sorry. I must have
transferred power

00:38:37.441 --> 00:38:38.430
from the holo-emitters.

00:38:38.475 --> 00:38:39.442
Well, be more careful.

00:38:39.476 --> 00:38:40.443
If I'm deactivated,

00:38:40.477 --> 00:38:42.069
this ship will never
get back to Starfleet.

00:38:42.112 --> 00:38:44.910
Okay, I'm taking power
from life support.

00:38:44.948 --> 00:38:47.246
We don't need that.
Try engines now.

00:38:48.285 --> 00:38:50.776
Nothing.
Why isn't this working?

00:38:50.821 --> 00:38:52.186
30 seconds to intercept.

00:38:52.222 --> 00:38:53.746
They're right on top of us.

00:38:53.790 --> 00:38:56.588
Hold it.
I see the problem.

00:38:56.627 --> 00:38:58.754
The thrust initiator
is off-line.

00:38:58.795 --> 00:38:59.955
- Stand by.
- 15 seconds.

00:39:00.063 --> 00:39:01.655
They're charging weapons!

00:39:01.698 --> 00:39:03.359
See if you can access
the shields.

00:39:03.400 --> 00:39:04.367
I said...

00:39:04.401 --> 00:39:05.527
I said shields...

00:39:05.569 --> 00:39:07.434
Already done. Shields up.

00:39:07.471 --> 00:39:10.804
This is the Warbird T'Met
calling the Prometheus.

00:39:12.309 --> 00:39:15.335
Commander Rekar... respond.

00:39:15.379 --> 00:39:16.812
Commander.

00:39:16.847 --> 00:39:19.509
This is the Prometheus.

00:39:19.549 --> 00:39:21.608
Activate your viewscreen.

00:39:22.986 --> 00:39:24.817
Our viewscreen
is not operational.

00:39:24.855 --> 00:39:27.722
We've had some trouble
with Starfleet commandos.

00:39:27.758 --> 00:39:29.419
Where's Rekar?

00:39:31.361 --> 00:39:32.350
In the medical bay.

00:39:32.396 --> 00:39:34.330
He suffered minor injuries.

00:39:34.364 --> 00:39:36.594
Identify yourself.

00:39:36.633 --> 00:39:37.827
You first.

00:39:37.868 --> 00:39:39.597
You first.

00:39:39.636 --> 00:39:41.627
Repeat your last statement.

00:39:41.672 --> 00:39:42.934
I don't understand.

00:39:42.973 --> 00:39:45.942
State your identity.

00:39:46.009 --> 00:39:47.636
This is Sub-Commander Almar.

00:39:47.678 --> 00:39:50.613
Lower your shields
and prepare to be boarded.

00:39:52.382 --> 00:39:54.282
They're already down.

00:39:54.318 --> 00:39:56.286
Maybe there's something wrong
with your sensor readings.

00:39:56.320 --> 00:39:57.617
You'd better not
try to transport

00:39:57.654 --> 00:39:58.882
until we can be sure it's safe.

00:39:58.922 --> 00:40:02.085
Lower your shields immediately,
or I'll open fire.

00:40:02.125 --> 00:40:03.752
Immediately?

00:40:03.794 --> 00:40:06.092
Yes. Prometheus out.

00:40:07.230 --> 00:40:08.822
Direct hit.

00:40:08.865 --> 00:40:10.799
Shields down to 20 percent.

00:40:11.935 --> 00:40:14.369
Three more ships
are approaching.

00:40:14.404 --> 00:40:15.769
We're doomed.

00:40:18.075 --> 00:40:19.099
No.

00:40:19.142 --> 00:40:20.905
They're Starfleet.

00:40:22.012 --> 00:40:23.604
What are they doing?

00:40:23.647 --> 00:40:24.944
Firing on us.

00:40:24.982 --> 00:40:26.677
They must think
Romulans are on board.

00:40:26.717 --> 00:40:27.809
They're right!

00:40:42.399 --> 00:40:45.368
Prometheus to any
Starfleet vessel. Respond.

00:40:45.402 --> 00:40:46.369
Prometheus...

00:40:46.403 --> 00:40:47.665
It's no use.
They can't hear us.

00:40:47.704 --> 00:40:49.331
The Romulans have scrambled
the com frequencies.

00:40:50.374 --> 00:40:53.639
Doctor, some... thing
just went off-line.

00:40:53.677 --> 00:40:54.905
Specifically?

00:40:54.945 --> 00:40:56.469
The secondary gyrodyne relays

00:40:56.513 --> 00:40:58.447
in the propulsion field
inter-matrix have depolarized.

00:40:58.482 --> 00:40:59.449
In English.

00:40:59.483 --> 00:41:01.451
I'm just reading
what it says here.

00:41:01.485 --> 00:41:03.248
I'll try to stabilize the ship.

00:41:03.286 --> 00:41:05.584
Transfer auxiliary power
to the maneuvering thrusters.

00:41:07.858 --> 00:41:10.349
Transferring auxiliary power
now.

00:41:12.095 --> 00:41:13.323
Good work, Mark-2.

00:41:13.363 --> 00:41:14.330
Thanks.

00:41:14.364 --> 00:41:15.592
You'd better get to tactical.

00:41:15.632 --> 00:41:17.099
We're going to have
to defend ourselves.

00:41:17.134 --> 00:41:18.829
Tactical. Right.

00:41:18.869 --> 00:41:19.836
What are you waiting for?

00:41:19.870 --> 00:41:21.030
Shoot.

00:41:22.205 --> 00:41:23.297
Shoot!

00:41:23.340 --> 00:41:25.069
There are so many controls.

00:41:25.108 --> 00:41:26.803
Find the one that says "fire"
and push it!

00:41:28.445 --> 00:41:29.639
It's not working.

00:41:29.679 --> 00:41:31.670
It says here
the phasers are off-line.

00:41:31.715 --> 00:41:32.943
Well, then fire a torpedo.

00:41:40.657 --> 00:41:42.147
You hit the wrong ship.

00:41:42.192 --> 00:41:43.523
It wasn't my fault.

00:41:43.560 --> 00:41:45.118
Well, then, whose fault was it,
the torpedo's?

00:41:45.162 --> 00:41:46.493
You're supposed
to tell it what to do.

00:41:48.365 --> 00:41:50.799
Navigational control
is off-line.

00:41:50.834 --> 00:41:53.132
Everything is off-line...
weapons, shields...

00:41:53.170 --> 00:41:54.159
It gets worse.

00:41:54.204 --> 00:41:56.263
There are two warbirds
coming right at us.

00:41:56.306 --> 00:41:58.831
My brilliant existence
cut short...

00:41:58.875 --> 00:42:00.502
No time to explore
the universe...

00:42:00.544 --> 00:42:02.307
no time to smell the roses...

00:42:02.345 --> 00:42:04.506
no time for... sex.

00:42:04.548 --> 00:42:07.813
Initiating decoupling sequence.

00:42:07.851 --> 00:42:08.818
What's that?

00:42:08.852 --> 00:42:10.183
What have I done now?

00:42:10.220 --> 00:42:12.211
Auto-separation in ten seconds.

00:42:12.255 --> 00:42:13.415
Auto-separation?

00:42:13.457 --> 00:42:15.254
I think the Romulans
did this before.

00:42:15.292 --> 00:42:16.384
How do we turn it off?

00:42:16.426 --> 00:42:17.654
I don't think we can.

00:42:17.694 --> 00:42:21.960
...Five, four, three, two...

00:42:22.032 --> 00:42:23.090
If I recall correctly,

00:42:23.133 --> 00:42:24.794
this next part gets
a little bumpy.

00:42:24.835 --> 00:42:26.700
Separation sequence in progress.

00:42:28.505 --> 00:42:30.666
Hold on.

00:42:30.707 --> 00:42:33.232
Specify attack pattern.

00:42:33.276 --> 00:42:35.642
Attack pattern... alpha?

00:42:35.679 --> 00:42:37.112
Specify target.

00:42:37.147 --> 00:42:38.705
- Romulans!
- Romulans!

00:42:48.024 --> 00:42:49.548
Bull's-eye!

00:42:49.593 --> 00:42:51.083
The warbirds are in retreat.

00:42:51.128 --> 00:42:52.595
Doctor, we've done it!

00:42:52.629 --> 00:42:54.756
Two holograms alone...

00:42:54.798 --> 00:42:56.925
Romulans on one side,
Starfleet on the other...

00:42:56.967 --> 00:42:58.662
alarms beeping everywhere.

00:42:58.702 --> 00:43:01.933
EMH-2... newborn
but filled with courage.

00:43:01.972 --> 00:43:04.941
EMH-1... armed
with years of experience.

00:43:04.975 --> 00:43:06.909
Together,
they emerged triumphant.

00:43:06.943 --> 00:43:08.342
The end.

00:43:09.546 --> 00:43:11.013
Or not.

00:43:15.418 --> 00:43:17.511
Welcome to the
Prometheus, gentlemen.

00:43:17.554 --> 00:43:18.543
It's about time.

00:43:25.061 --> 00:43:27.894
I'm receiving a transmission
through the sensor network.

00:43:27.931 --> 00:43:29.421
Origin...

00:43:29.466 --> 00:43:31.093
the Alpha Quadrant.

00:43:32.502 --> 00:43:34.697
Does it contain
a holographic subroutine?

00:43:35.939 --> 00:43:37.406
Yes.

00:43:37.440 --> 00:43:38.930
Transfer it to Sick Bay.

00:43:38.975 --> 00:43:40.340
Torres to Bridge.

00:43:40.377 --> 00:43:43.039
Captain, I think he's back.

00:43:59.696 --> 00:44:01.459
Doctor...

00:44:01.498 --> 00:44:03.295
report.

00:44:03.333 --> 00:44:06.097
I... I did it.

00:44:06.136 --> 00:44:08.070
You completed the mission?

00:44:08.104 --> 00:44:10.800
Yes. Once the Romulans
were out of the way.

00:44:10.840 --> 00:44:11.807
Romulans?

00:44:11.841 --> 00:44:13.103
They'd taken over

00:44:13.143 --> 00:44:14.906
the Prometheus...
the ship I was on.

00:44:14.945 --> 00:44:17.038
But I managed
to turn the tables on them

00:44:17.080 --> 00:44:18.638
with a little help
from a fellow EMH.

00:44:18.682 --> 00:44:20.411
You got through to Starfleet?

00:44:20.450 --> 00:44:22.179
I spoke directly
with Headquarters.

00:44:22.219 --> 00:44:25.711
Apparently, Voyager
was declared officially lost

00:44:25.755 --> 00:44:26.949
14 months ago.

00:44:27.023 --> 00:44:28.650
I set the record straight.

00:44:28.692 --> 00:44:31.627
I told them everything
that's happened to this crew.

00:44:31.661 --> 00:44:33.629
They said they would
contact your families

00:44:33.663 --> 00:44:35.494
to tell them the news
and promised

00:44:35.532 --> 00:44:38.194
that they won't stop
until they've found a way

00:44:38.235 --> 00:44:39.759
to get Voyager back home.

00:44:41.571 --> 00:44:44.563
And they asked me
to relay a message.

00:44:45.875 --> 00:44:48.639
They wanted you to know...

00:44:48.678 --> 00:44:50.839
you're no longer alone.

00:44:54.884 --> 00:44:57.648
60,000 light-years

00:44:57.687 --> 00:45:00.713
seems a little closer today.
